{#
  Who We Are. Composes the frame and the locked components; copy lives in front
  matter. Three notes for review:

  1. NO alt-glyph on any headline here. The handoff swaps the A in the "The
     Team" h2, but design.md section 3 requires each swap to be justified by
     what that specific word MEANS, and a crossbar-less A says nothing about a
     team. It was available, not meaningful, so it is dropped.

     The one swap that remains is the A in "Circulation" in the name-origin
     list. That is not a headline swap: it is the wordmark itself, quoted as
     the term being defined, and design.md section 9 locks the crossbar-less A
     into the wordmark in every setting. Rendering it plain there would show a
     wordmark the brand does not use.

  2. This page carries Alex Loveless's FULL testimonial, the relationship
     account. The home page carries the short pull quote drawn from it. They
     are different treatments of the same source and must not be swapped or
     duplicated.

  3. The bilingual notes in three team members' roles are the team's language
     capability, which is real and stays. It describes the PEOPLE. It is not a
     signal that the site should be bilingual; see the language decision in
     SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md.
#}
{% from "components/container.njk" import container %}
{% from "components/section.njk" import section %}
{% from "components/button.njk" import button %}

{% call section() %}
  <h1 class="cs-opening__headline">{{ opening.headline }}</h1>
  <p class="cs-opening__lede">{{ opening.lede }}</p>
{% endcall %}

{% call container(class="pb-24") %}
  <h2 class="cs-teamhead">The Team</h2>
  <ul class="cs-teamgrid">
    {% for member in team %}
      <li class="cs-member">
        {# Portrait ground stays blank until real photography lands. Adding a
           `photo` to this member in front matter swaps the image in with no
           markup change. #}
        <div class="cs-portrait">
          {% if member.photo %}
            <img class="cs-portrait__img"
                 src="{{ site.cdn }}{{ member.photo }}"
                 alt="{{ member.name }}, {{ member.role }}"
                 width="340" height="400" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          {% endif %}
          <span class="cs-portrait__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>
        <p class="cs-member__specialty">{{ member.specialty }}</p>
        <p class="cs-member__name">{{ member.name }}</p>
        <p class="cs-member__role">{{ member.role }}</p>
        <p class="cs-member__bio">{{ member.bio }}</p>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

<div class="cs-graft">
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--graft cs-rule--graft-l" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--graft cs-rule--graft-r" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {% call container(class="relative") %}
    <img class="cs-graft__figure"
         src="{{ site.cdn }}cs-img-graft-square.webp"
         alt="Graft, two stems joined into one stronger stem"
         width="1120" height="560" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <div class="cs-graft__tick" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {% endcall %}
</div>

{% call container(narrow=true, class="pt-24") %}
  <p class="cs-eyebrow">In a client’s words</p>
  <blockquote class="cs-testimonial">
    <p>{{ testimonial.body }}</p>
    <cite>{{ testimonial.cite }}</cite>
  </blockquote>
{% endcall %}

{% call container(narrow=true, class="py-24") %}
  <p class="cs-eyebrow cs-eyebrow--center">Why the name</p>
  <dl class="cs-origin">
    {% for entry in origin %}
      <div class="cs-origin__group">
        <dt class="cs-origin__term">
          {%- if entry.term == "Circulation" -%}
            Circul<span class="alt-soft">a</span>tion
          {%- else -%}
            {{ entry.term }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </dt>
        <dd class="cs-origin__def">{{ entry.definition }}</dd>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </dl>
{% endcall %}

{% call container(class="cs-close") %}
  <p class="cs-close__note">{{ close }}</p>
  {{ button("Start a conversation", href="/contact/") }}
{% endcall %}
